. esttab using "$drive\tabs\Extensive1.tex", se keep(hchoice mchoice round) scalars("hasfe Fixed Effect" "hascon Controls") nomtitles mgroups("Hypothesis 1" "Hypothesis 2", pattern(1 0 0 1 0) ///
>   prefix(\multicolumn{c -(}@span{c )-}{c -(}c{c )-}{c -(}) suffix({c )-}) span) ///
>        nonotes addnote("Linear OLS regressions using a binary measure for whetehr or not a participant donated at all as a dependent variable. There are two treatment variables: the Options variable measures whether they could see 40 charities versus 5; the Choices variable measures whether they could select multiple charities to donate to versus just one. Individual fixed effects can be included for the Options treatment because there is within-participant variation in the number of charities seen, but the Choices treatment is between-participant. Regressions exclude the default arm of the experiment, which measures whether the participant has a pre-selected donation option, and the perceived importance arm, which measures whether the participant can see the number of charities devoted to a cause before selecting that cause. Covariates include education level, race, marital status, employment status, religion, income, age, and gender." "Standard errors in parentheses, clustered by individual" "\sym{c -(}*{c )-} \(p<0.10\), \sym{c -(}**{c )-} \(p<0.05\), \sym{c -(}***{c )-} \(p<0.01\)" ) ///
>  alignment(c) label replace ///
>       title (Effect of Treatments on Donations \label{c -(}TableExtensive1{c )-}) 
